 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Night sky; geometric for «بل إياه تدعون». No idols, no illness, no Shaytan drawn. Al-Muyassar's first-person «بعثنا… ابتليناهم… لنا» not used. STAGING v4: 40-41 stay ambient (a hypothetical addressed to the idolaters and His answering the call: no gesture inside the condition). 42-43: an earlier nation (three men in dark robes; an uncountable crowd behind rocks would read as troops) in fields at dusk; they shake their heads on 42:4 (As-Sa'di: they denied the messengers, who are not drawn); a falling-leaf plate on 42:8 and a dusty gust on 42:9 for the hardship (Al-Muyassar: poverty and hard living; As-Sa'di: poverty, blights); the fields are not destroyed; no illness and no one hurt; no humbling gesture on 42:10-43:5 (they did not humble themselves); they turn on 43:7 (hearts hardened); Satan is not drawn; a two-paths plate on 43:9."
 },
